# Ant Design Quick Start Tutorial

Ant Design (antd) is a React UI library that provides high-quality components and demos for building rich, interactive user interfaces. This tutorial will help you get started quickly with Ant Design.

## Table of Contents
- [Installation](#installation)
- [Basic Setup](#basic-setup)
- [Your First Component](#your-first-component)
- [Common Components](#common-components)
- [Layout Components](#layout-components)
- [Form Components](#form-components)
- [Navigation Components](#navigation-components)
- [Feedback Components](#feedback-components)
- [Customization](#customization)
- [Best Practices](#best-practices)
- [Resources](#resources)

## Installation

### Using npm
```bash
npm install antd
```

### Using yarn
```bash
yarn add antd
```

### Using pnpm
```bash
pnpm add antd
```

## Basic Setup

### 1. Import CSS
In your main entry file (e.g., `src/index.js` or `src/main.js`):

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import 'antd/dist/reset.css'; // Import Ant Design styles
import App from './App';

const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root'));
root.render(<App />);
```

### 2. Configure for Vite (if using Vite)
If you're using Vite, you might need to configure it to handle CSS imports properly:

```javascript
// vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  css: {
    preprocessorOptions: {
      less: {
        javascriptEnabled: true,
      },
    },
  },
});
```

## Your First Component

Here's a simple example using a Button component:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Button } from 'antd';

function App() {
  return (
    <div style={{ padding: '20px' }}>
      <h1>Welcome to Ant Design!</h1>
      <Button type="primary">Click Me</Button>
      <Button>Default Button</Button>
      <Button type="dashed">Dashed</Button>
      <Button type="text">Text Button</Button>
      <Button type="link">Link</Button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

## Common Components

### Button
```jsx
import { Button } from 'antd';

function ButtonExample() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Button type="primary">Primary</Button>
      <Button type="default">Default</Button>
      <Button type="dashed">Dashed</Button>
      <Button type="text">Text</Button>
      <Button type="link">Link</Button>

      <Button danger>Danger</Button>
      <Button disabled>Disabled</Button>
      <Button loading>Loading</Button>

      <Button shape="circle">A</Button>
      <Button shape="round">Rounded</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Typography
```jsx
import { Typography } from 'antd';

const { Title, Paragraph, Text } = Typography;

function TypographyExample() {
  return (
    <Typography>
      <Title>Level 1 Title</Title>
      <Title level={2}>Level 2 Title</Title>
      <Title level={3}>Level 3 Title</Title>
      <Title level={4}>Level 4 Title</Title>

