TITLE: Implement Next.js Root Middleware with Path-Based Logic
DESCRIPTION: This TypeScript code demonstrates how to consolidate multiple Next.js middleware functionalities into a single root `middleware.ts` file. It leverages `NextRequest` to inspect the incoming URL's pathname, allowing conditional execution of specific logic blocks for different routes like `/about` or `/dashboard`. This pattern is the recommended approach for managing middleware in Next.js, replacing the deprecated nested middleware structure.

SOURCE: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/errors/nested-middleware.mdx#_snippet_0

LANGUAGE: TypeScript
CODE:
```
import type { NextRequest } from 'next/server'

export function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
  if (request.nextUrl.pathname.startsWith('/about')) {
    // This logic is only applied to /about
  }

  if (request.nextUrl.pathname.startsWith('/dashboard')) {
    // This logic is only applied to /dashboard
  }
}
```

